    "title": "How to watch the Masters today, Round 4 start time, TV schedule",
    "text": "If the final round is anything like the third round, we're in for a wild ride Sunday at the 2026 Masters.Rory McIlroy and Cameron Young share the lead entering the last day of competition, with a host of big names within striking distance, all looking to secure a Green Jacket and become immortalized as a Masters champion.AdvertisementBelow, you'll find everything you need to know about Sunday's final round of the Masters, including TV and streaming information, tee times and betting odds.SCORES: Masters 2026 leaderboard, tee times, videosRory McIlroy of Northern Ireland acknowledges the crowd on the 18th green during the second round of the 2026 Masters Tournament at Augusta National Golf Club on April 10, 2026 in Augusta, Georgia.What channel is the Masters on today? Time, TV scheduleAll times EasternCoverage of the 2026 Masters final round will begin Sunday at 12 p.m. ET on Paramount+ before moving to CBS at 2 p.m. until the end of play. You can stream the CBS broadcast on Paramount+ or Fubo, which includes a free trial for new subscribers.Where to watch 2026 Masters on streamingHere's a look at the Masters final round alternate feeds streaming on Sunday:AdvertisementAll times EasternOn the Range (10 a.m.-12 p.m.)Featured groups (10:15 a.m.-7 p.m.)Holes 4, 5 and 6 (10 a.m.-3:30 p.m.)Amen Corner (11:45 a.m.-6 p.m.)Inside Amen Corner (11:45 a.m.-6 p.m.)Holes 15 and 16 (Holes 15 & 16)Masters tee times todayRory McIlroy and Cameron Young tee off in the final pairing at 2:25 p.m. ET on Sunday. Check out the full tee sheet here.Masters final round betting oddsRory McIlroy is the slight favorite to win his second straight Masters title Sunday. See the full list of odds here.This article originally appeared on Golfweek: Where to watch Masters 2026, TV coverage, streaming for final round",
